          "The `transfer` function can also return `true` even if the inherited token implementation changes `_transfer` to return a status value.",
          "The `mint` function correctly applies `onlyOwner` and uses `_mint(to, amount)`, which increases the recipient’s balance and updates total supply under standard ERC-20 behavior.",
          "The `burn` function correctly burns tokens from `msg.sender`; callers must approve the contract if the token uses allowance-based burning in a separate function.",
          "There is no obvious performance problem in these functions.",
          "Clarity would improve if the code documented the blacklist policy directly in the contract."
